It's one of the optional gifts you can get from praying on an altar. 
There is a chance that you hear a voice say 'Hark, mortal!  To enter
the castle, thou must play the right tune!'

If this happens, the next time you safely pray on an altar, 'You hear
a divine music...  It sounds like:  AAAAA' where AAAAA is the passtune
for that game.  Then, since you know it, if you play a musical
instrument at the right place and don't improvise, you will be asked
if you want to play the passtune, much like you are asked if you have
discovered the tune by yourself.

It used to be a much bigger deal for me before I learned how to divine
the tune myself (I actually had the gears and tumblers messages
switched!).  Now, I personally find the other divine gifts to be much
more valuable, and am somewhat disappointed if all I get is the castle
tune.  If you do it the right way, you can be assured of getting the
passtune in no more than 16 turns...

