Play AAAAA, BBBBB, CCCCC, DDDDD, EEEEE, FFFFF to determine how many of
each note A-G are in the tune, stopping when you know all five notes. 
Let's assume BCDEG are the notes in some order...

Now, pick a note not in the tune as a place holder, in our example, A.
 Play BAAAA, ABAAA, and so on until you know which position B falls
in.  This should take no more than 4 tries, as if the first four fail,
B is the fifth note.

Repeat this step with each of the other good notes, skipping known
notes until all have been identified.  If you are most unlucky (you,
not your character), you will need all 6 same note sequences to get
the correct notes, then 4+3+2+1 turns to figure out where each note
goes... 16 turns.

